-- English names for the seeded foods (#351). User decision A+ (2026-11-27): the public foods (005),
-- the franchise foods (013) and the Bibigo foods (014) get English names, brands and categories,
-- for example "Jajangmyeon (black bean noodles)" in "Noodles and dumplings". The old Korean
-- "brand name" text moves into search_alias, which only the food search reads and no screen or API
-- response shows, so a Korean search (the dish name, or the brand and name) still finds the food.
-- Foods a person added keep their own text: only a row that still has a seeded Korean name and
-- brand is renamed. A category is renamed only while it still has its seeded value.
-- Running it again changes nothing, because the renamed rows no longer match the Korean names.
-- A seeded row stays Korean if the person already added a food with the English name and brand,
-- since (name, brand) must stay unique.
--
-- Replaying the seed files 005, 013 and 014 on a database that already ran this file (the migration
-- check does it) inserts the Korean rows again. A Korean row whose renamed twin exists with the same
-- alias, and that no meal or combo uses, is such a replay copy, so it is deleted before the rename.

ALTER TABLE foods ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS search_alias text;

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS seed_food_names;
